From 4f85b7dd5eaa77d986f9fdc7f8f46f3d2fe06261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:27:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/35] dns: retransmit plain UDP queries while no answer has
 come

Our fresh-socket exchange sent a query once and waited for its deadline.
The DNS client folds duplicate questions into the exchange in flight, so
the retries of clients (dnsmasq) never reached the server: one lost
datagram cost the whole deadline.

The same datagram, on the same socket with the same ID, is sent again at
1 s and 3 s while no answer has come (at most three sends, RFC 9520), and
an answer to any of them is taken (RFC 1035 7.3). Every caller keeps its
own deadline as its policy: the main exchange, the provider probe
(1.5 s, two sends), the provider race (losers cancelled at once; the race
now waits for them before it returns), the background probe.
---
 dns/client_fallback_provider.go |  10 +-
 dns/exchange_fresh.go           |  22 +++-
 dns/exchange_fresh_test.go      | 174 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 dns/exchange_fresh_test.go

